+### Native workspace trust (2026-10-05)
+
+Refreshed on macOS 26.3 arm64 with tmux, Cursor CLI `2026.07.17-3e2a980` retained in its versioned installation, and stable launcher `2026.10.01-e373342`.
+These versions restrict `--trust` to print/headless mode, superseding the older interactive launch-flag observation below.
+Interactive spawn and relaunch omit that flag and use the native workspace action implemented in `bin/fm-cursor-lib.sh`.
+The live guard starts Cursor in fresh scratch repositories on a private tmux socket, proves real `comm cursor` process ancestry, answers the displayed action, and requires a worker to read its positional brief and append the exact status it specifies.
+It exercises both a plain workspace and a workspace carrying an unapproved local MCP configuration.
+Both installed versions displayed only `[a] Trust this workspace` in those launches; neither offered `[w]`, so workspace-only MCP approval remains portable-regression coverage rather than a live claim for these versions.
+No fixture MCP server ran.
+
+Refresh with the retained version and then the stable launcher:
+
+```sh
+FM_CURSOR_TRUST_LIVE=1 \
+  FM_CURSOR_BIN="$HOME/.local/share/cursor-agent/versions/2026.07.17-3e2a980/cursor-agent" \
+  FM_CURSOR_TRUST_LAB_ROOT="$PWD/config" \
+  bash bin/fm-test-run.sh tests/fm-cursor-trust-live-e2e.test.sh
+FM_CURSOR_TRUST_LIVE=1 FM_CURSOR_TRUST_LAB_ROOT="$PWD/config" \
+  bash bin/fm-test-run.sh tests/fm-cursor-trust-live-e2e.test.sh
+```
+
+The retained-version output was:
+
+```text
+# Cursor 2026.07.17-3e2a980
+ok - Cursor 2026.07.17-3e2a980: real process ancestry identifies comm cursor (plain)
+ok - Cursor 2026.07.17-3e2a980: plain [a] approval reached positional brief and status append
+# Cursor 2026.07.17-3e2a980: MCP-configured launch did not offer [w]; exercising its displayed [a] dialog instead
+ok - Cursor 2026.07.17-3e2a980: real process ancestry identifies comm cursor (mcp)
+ok - Cursor 2026.07.17-3e2a980: mcp [a] approval reached positional brief and status append
+# all Cursor native trust live checks passed (2)
+```
+
+The stable-launcher run also exited 0 and ended with:
+
+```text
+ok - Cursor 2026.10.01-e373342: real process ancestry identifies comm cursor (mcp)
+ok - Cursor 2026.10.01-e373342: mcp [a] approval reached positional brief and status append
+# all Cursor native trust live checks passed (2)
