+
+The displayed trust dialog has two independent identifying lines, `Workspace Trust Required` and `Do you trust the contents of this directory?`, and a named `[a]` action.
+After approval, Cursor can retain the completed card above its conversation with `Trusting workspace...` replacing its navigation hint.
+The readiness gate distinguishes that completed card from an unanswered dialog and requires the processing footer or this task's new conversation transcript.
+It reads only the viewport and fails with the installed Cursor version if capture or processing confirmation fails.
+Backends without a verified viewport primitive, currently cmux and Orca, are refused before launch.
+Portable coverage in `tests/fm-cursor-harness.test.sh` and `tests/fm-spawn-dispatch-profile.test.sh` pins independent dialog identifiers, named actions, workspace-only MCP selection, completed cards, task-bound transcripts, stale scrollback, unreadable captures, and stalled endpoints.
+On macOS installations that cannot execute copied system Bash, the portable ancestry construction reports an explicit skip; the real Cursor ancestry guard above supplies its positive counterpart.
